{
    "version": "1.9.13",
    "changelog": "Two things. (1) NEW \u2014 the building jump. Buildings now show on the main map as roof-coloured blocks (the same picture as the satellite view), and clicking a building asks 'Edit this location?' \u2014 answer yes and the Building Editor opens on that building. A click that drags (panning) never asks; clicking a road still just selects the road; and cancelling the question changes nothing. If the Building Editor is not installed, the editor says so plainly. (The Building Editor learns to receive the jump in its own next update \u2014 its receiving half is built and tested, and until it ships the handoff is still prepared.) (2) SAVE FIX: when a save changes a zone's roads, the editor now also updates the map manifest (detailed/map-manifest.json) in the same save \u2014 the changed files' fingerprints and sizes are refreshed and the map version steps up \u2014 so the game actually downloads the roads you just saved. That missing step is why the joins saved on Oct 25 never reached the game until the manifest was repaired by hand.",
